{"name":"Wake Me Up","hex":"#f6d559","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["(often followed by up) To stop sleeping.","(often followed by up) To make somebody stop sleeping; to rouse from sleep."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period after a person's death before or after the body is buried, cremated, etc.; in some cultures accompanied by a party or collectively sorting through the deceased's personal effects.","The state of forbearing sleep, especially for solemn or festive purposes; a vigil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wake Me Up (Girls Aloud song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wake Me Up\" is a song recorded by British girl group Girls Aloud from their second studio album, What Will the Neighbours Say? (2004). It was released by Polydor Records on 21 February 2005, as the fourth and final single from the album. The song had been initially considered as the lead single, however, it was deemed to sound too harsh and the record company did not want to take the risk. The track was written by Miranda Cooper, Brian Higgins, Tim Powell, Shawn Lee, Lisa Cowling, Paul Woods and Yusra Maru'e. \"Wake Me Up\" is a pop rock song composed of a \"garage rock guitar riff\". It received mixed reviews from music critics. While some described it as predictable, others wrote that it appeared to be an attempt to recapture the sound of some of their previous release. Alex Kapranos, the lead singer of indie rock band Franz Ferdinand, said \"Wake Me Up\" inspired the band to work with producer Brian Higgins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg/330px-WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wake_Me_Up_(Girls_Aloud_song)"},{"title":"Wake Me Up (Avicii song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wake Me Up\" is a song by Swedish DJ and record producer Avicii. It was released as the lead single from his debut album True on 17 June 2013, by PRMD Music and Island Records. It was written by Avicii, Mike Einziger of Incubus, and American soul singer Aloe Blacc, who provides vocals for the track. Mike Einziger provides acoustic guitar, while Peter Dyer provides keyboard on the song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wake_Me_Up_(Avicii_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg/330px-WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg/330px-WakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWakeMeUpCoverCD2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/da/Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png/250px-Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/da/Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png/250px-Avicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAvicii_Wake_Me_Up_Official_Single_Cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Aloe_Blacc_-_Wake_Me_Up.jpg/250px-Aloe_Blacc_-_Wake_Me_Up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo